This is a Neovim configuration built on LazyVim. It includes custom plugins in dev/.

## Key Facts

- Entry point: init.lua → lua/config/lazy.lua (bootstraps lazy.nvim + LazyVim)
- Plugin specs live in lua/plugins/ (each file returns a lazy.nvim spec table)
- Custom plugins: dev/adbhelper.nvim (Android/iOS device actions) and dev/reviewbuddy.nvim (unified Herdr/cmux review comments)
- Leader key: , (comma)
- Lua style: 2-space indent, 120 column width (stylua.toml)
- Format with: stylua lua/
- nvim-lint is explicitly disabled
- kotlin_language_server is disabled; Treesitter fallback used for Kotlin symbols

## Writing Plugin Code

- Use vim.uv (not vim.loop) for async I/O — this config targets Neovim 0.10+
- Custom plugins load via event = "VeryLazy" plus explicit cmd/keys tables
- adbhelper.nvim uses pure Lua + Neovim APIs for Android/iOS device actions
- reviewbuddy.nvim uses pure Lua + Neovim APIs, depends on folke/snacks.nvim for its comment float, detects whether Neovim is hosted by Herdr, Herdr app, or cmux, discovers targets only in that host's current workspace/space, sends Herdr app prompts with `hc`, and pastes/submits only to sibling cmux terminals with an unambiguous foreground agent process when no hook-backed receiver exists
- New reviewbuddy.nvim clients implement the internal adapter contract in `dev/reviewbuddy.nvim/lua/reviewbuddy/backends/` and follow `dev/reviewbuddy.nvim/docs/backends.md`; do not add client switches to `targets.lua` or `submit.lua`

## Environment

- LazyVim extras: editor.outline, lang.java, lang.json, lang.kotlin, lang.markdown
